## 2. Schéma Relationnel de la Base de Données  

**Entités principales**  

| Table | PK | Colonnes clés | FK | Relation |
|-------|----|---------------|----|----------|
| users | id (UUID) | email, password_hash, name, driver_license_number, created_at, updated_at | — | 1‑N → rentals |
| cars | id (UUID) | make, model, year, license_plate, daily_rate, status (available/rented/maintenance), created_at, updated_at | — | 1‑N → rentals |
| rentals | id (UUID) | user_id, car_id, start_date, end_date, total_price, status (reserved/active/completed/cancelled), created_at, updated_at | user_id → users.id (N‑1) <br> car_id → cars.id (N‑1) | N‑1 (users) <br> N‑1 (cars) |
| payments | id (UUID) | rental_id, amount, payment_method, payment_date, status, created_at, updated_at | rental_id → rentals.id (N‑1) | N‑1 → rentals |
| locations | id (UUID) | address_line, city, postal_code, country, latitude, longitude, created_at, updated_at | — | 1‑N → cars (optional, if car linked to location) |
| car_images | id (UUID) | car_id, url, alt_text, created_at, updated_at | car_id → cars.id (N‑1) | N‑1 → cars |
| audit_logs | id (UUID) | user_id, action, entity_type, entity_id, timestamp, details | user_id → users.id (N‑1) | N‑1 → users |

**Relations**  

- users 1‑N rentals  
- cars 1‑N rentals  
- rentals 1‑N payments  
- cars 1‑N car_images  
- (optionnel) locations 1‑N cars  

